%U A399123 233289,239121,263169,269361,271441,275625,277729,281961,291600,313600,330625,562500,722500,837225,893025,1071225,1092025,1134225
%N A399123 Squares that are the concatenation of a prime and a square.
%C A399123 If k is a term, then so is 100*k.
%H A399123 Robert Israel, <a href="/A399123/b399123.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..7300</a>
%e A399123 a(3) = 1936 is a term because 1936 = 44^2 is a square and the concatenation of the prime 19 and the square 36 = 6^2.
%e A399123 The first term that is the concatenation of a prime and a square in more than one way is a(40) = 1134225 = 1065^2, which is the concatenation of 11 and 34225 = 185^2 and of 113 and 4225 = 65^2.
%p A399123 f:= proc(s) local n,k,r;
%p A399123   n:= s^2;
%p A399123   for k from 1 to ilog10(n) do
%p A399123     r:= n mod 10^k;
%p A399123     if r >= 10^(k-1) and issqr(r) and isprime((n-r)/10^k) then return n fi;
%p A399123   od;
%p A399123 NULL
%p A399123 end proc:
%p A399123 map(f, [seq(i^2, i=1..10^4)]);
%Y A399123 Cf. A300105.
%K A399123 nonn,base,new
%O A399123 1,1
%A A399123 _Robert Israel_, Aug 19 2026
